    "description": "Costs a bit more than a developer, and the hire is a gamble for morale. A good manager lifts happiness; a poor one drags it down. While they are here, the next developer is more likely to be a good hire, and a small refactor stays on the schedule. Recruiting takes 14 days and $2,500 up front; payroll starts when they do. Once they start, Keep the lights on rises by $35/day.",
    "ktloPerDay": 35,
    "category": "change-structure",
    "human": true,
    "delayDays": 14,
    "cost": {
      "oneTime": 2500,
      "perDay": 500
